[[00:15:41]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZIcVQwZEnqA&t=941s) >> Thank you, Mr. Chairman. Julie Anthony, victim assistance coordinator for the Cheyenne Police Department. Uh through you, sir.

[[00:15:54]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZIcVQwZEnqA&t=954s) Can you hear me? Okay, sir. It's the goal of the Cheyenne Police Department victim assistance program to provide services that facilitate the physical and emotional recovery of victims of crime in our community. Victim assistance advocates provide trauma-informed services to victims of crime and those services include ongoing

[[00:16:11]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZIcVQwZEnqA&t=971s) case management, connection to community

[[00:16:14]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZIcVQwZEnqA&t=974s) resources such as housing, mental health

[[00:16:17]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZIcVQwZEnqA&t=977s) counseling, crime victim compensation,

[[00:16:20]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZIcVQwZEnqA&t=980s) social support services, and child care resources. We also provide individualized safety planning, direct victims to medical care, accompany victims to medical appointments and medical forensic exams,

[[00:16:34]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZIcVQwZEnqA&t=994s) and provide onseen support for victims in crisis. The rapid support model our department utilizes is crucial for victims of crime

[[00:16:43]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZIcVQwZEnqA&t=1003s) as rapid advocacy support of victims

[[00:16:47]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZIcVQwZEnqA&t=1007s) lessens the likelihood that they'll experience severe long-term mental

[[00:16:51]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZIcVQwZEnqA&t=1011s) health concerns as a result of their victimization. Advocates are often the first line of defense in identifying suicidality and

[[00:17:00]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZIcVQwZEnqA&t=1020s) providing intervention and mental health support. Rapid advocacy support allows victims to

[[00:17:08]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZIcVQwZEnqA&t=1028s) access urgent financial assistance that

[[00:17:11]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZIcVQwZEnqA&t=1031s) forestalls long-term ramifications such

[[00:17:13]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZIcVQwZEnqA&t=1033s) as eviction, job loss, and aggravated

[[00:17:16]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZIcVQwZEnqA&t=1036s) health concerns due to lack of financial

[[00:17:19]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZIcVQwZEnqA&t=1039s) access to medical care. Ongoing case

[[00:17:23]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZIcVQwZEnqA&t=1043s) management gives victims of crime one

[[00:17:25]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZIcVQwZEnqA&t=1045s) consistent point of contact within the police department or handling their cases. and that avoids confusion and

[[00:17:33]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZIcVQwZEnqA&t=1053s) allows information to be made more readily available to both victims of crime and investigating officers.

[[00:17:41]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZIcVQwZEnqA&t=1061s) During the previous 2-year grant cycle,

[[00:17:44]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZIcVQwZEnqA&t=1064s) Cheyenne Police Department victim assistance provided 1,486

[[00:17:49]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZIcVQwZEnqA&t=1069s) victims of crime with 1,918

[[00:17:52]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZIcVQwZEnqA&t=1072s) instances of service.

[[00:17:55]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZIcVQwZEnqA&t=1075s) 196 instances of unseen crisis response

[[00:17:58]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZIcVQwZEnqA&t=1078s) or crisis intervention were also provided. Victim assistance services are crucial for the support and recovery of crime victims in the city of Cheyenne. State

[[00:18:10]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZIcVQwZEnqA&t=1090s) division of victim services funding assists in these efforts and it is for this reason that I respectfully request that the city council approve this resolution. I thank you for your time and consideration and I'm happy to answer any questions you may have. >> Thank you. Uh any questions for Miss Anthony from the committee?

